    "custom_liquid_t4pnL4": {
      "type": "custom-liquid",
      "settings": {
        "custom_liquid": "<style>\n  /* General Styling */\n  .rma-container {\n    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n    line-height: 1.6;\n    color: #333;\n    max-width: 800px;\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    padding: 20px;\n    background: white;\n    border-radius: 10px;\n    box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);\n  }\n\n  .rma-container h1 {\n    font-size: 28px;\n    color: #2c3e50;\n    text-align: center;\n    margin-bottom: 20px;\n    background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgb(139 214 218), rgb(166 236 208));\n    -webkit-background-clip: text;\n    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;\n  }\n\n  .rma-container h2 {\n    font-size: 24px;\n    color: #2c3e50;\n    margin-top: 30px;\n    margin-bottom: 15px;\n    padding-bottom: 5px;\n    border-bottom: 2px solid rgb(139 214 218);\n  }\n\n  .rma-container h3 {\n    font-size: 20px;\n    color: #2c3e50;\n    margin-top: 25px;\n    margin-bottom: 10px;\n  }\n\n  .rma-container p {\n    font-size: 16px;\n    margin-bottom: 15px;\n  }\n\n  .rma-container ul {\n    margin-bottom: 15px;\n    padding-left: 20px;\n  }\n\n  .rma-container ul li {\n    margin-bottom: 10px;\n  }\n\n  .rma-container table {\n    width: 100%;\n    border-collapse: collapse;\n    margin-bottom: 20px;\n  }\n\n  .rma-container table th,\n  .rma-container table td {\n    padding: 10px;\n    border: 1px solid #ddd;\n    text-align: left;\n  }\n\n  .rma-container table th {\n    background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgb(139 214 218), rgb(166 236 208));\n    color: white;\n    font-weight: bold;\n  }\n\n  .rma-container table tr:nth-child(even) {\n    background-color: #f9f9f9;\n  }\n\n  .rma-container table tr:hover {\n    background-color: rgba(139, 214, 218, 0.1);\n  }\n\n  .rma-container .note {\n    background-color: #f8f9fa;\n    padding: 15px;\n    border-left: 4px solid rgb(139 214 218);\n    margin-bottom: 20px;\n    font-size: 14px;\n    color: #555;\n  }\n\n  /* Responsive Design */\n  @media (max-width: 768px) {\n    .rma-container {\n      padding: 15px;\n    }\n\n    .rma-container h1 {\n      font-size: 24px;\n    }\n\n    .rma-container h2 {\n      font-size: 20px;\n    }\n\n    .rma-container h3 {\n      font-size: 18px;\n    }\n\n    .rma-container p {\n      font-size: 14px;\n    }\n\n    .rma-container table th,\n    .rma-container table td {\n      padding: 8px;\n    }\n  }\n</style>\n\n<div class=\"rma-container\">\n  <h1>RMA (Return Merchandise Authorization)</h1>\n\n  <h2>What is RMA?</h2>\n  <p>RMA stands for “Return Merchandise Authorization”. This is the process we use to handle and manage the return of products, such as defective or wrongly delivered products. Customers must request an RMA through their customer account.</p>\n\n  <h2>How to Create RMA?</h2>\n  <p>We have established several guidelines for creating an RMA. To submit an RMA, you will need to go through the steps of our process. Learn about the process we use to handle and manage our RMAs here:</p>\n\n  <h2>Warranty Information</h2>\n  <table>\n    <thead>\n      <tr>\n        <th>Product Group</th>\n        <th>Warranty</th>\n      </tr>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr>\n        <td>Spareparts</td>\n        <td>Lifetime</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>Service Packs</td>\n        <td>3 Months</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>Batteries</td>\n        <td>12 Months</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>Tools</td>\n        <td>12 Months</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>Accesories</td>\n        <td>12 Months</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>Premium Accesories (Baseus, Canyon, Aeno, Prestigio, Rixus)</td>\n        <td>24 Months</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>New devices (Phones/Laptop)</td>\n        <td>Factory Warranty (36 Months)</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>Refurbished devices (Phones)</td>\n        <td>3 Months</td>\n      </tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n  <div class=\"note\">\n    *It is very important to thoroughly test and review the product(s) before installation!\n  </div>\n\n  <h2>What is Not Covered by Warranty?</h2>\n  <p>We cannot accept products under our warranty in the following cases:</p>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Products that do not have our stamp or labels</li>\n    <li>Products that are already installed but were never tested beforehand</li>\n    <li>Incorrectly bent cables</li>\n    <li>Damage caused by tampering, improper use, and carelessness</li>\n    <li>Physical defects or damages</li>\n    <li>Defects and damage caused by accident</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>General Return Conditions</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Make sure the return is registered in your account.</li>\n    <li>Customers must test and inspect the product before installation. Our RMA department has several techniques that allow them to identify whether a product has been installed before it has been tested.</li>\n    <li>When sending your RMA, make clear on the outside of the box that it’s an RMA shipment, this fastens the process.</li>\n    <li>Products must have been purchased from 4Phones (proved by stickers/labels/stamps).</li>\n    <li>Products must be returned in their original condition and packaging. If this is not the case, we may reject the product or charge a reduction in value. Please do not write or put stickers on the products or packaging.</li>\n    <li>The product should not be damaged (for example, due to incorrect installation). The RMA department will determine the condition of the returned product.</li>\n    <li>Please note that all products have an established warranty period. The term varies by product group, see the table above under the heading 'warranty'.</li>\n    <li>Please note that we will refund the current market value upon receipt of the goods or exchange it for a new product.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>How to Avoid Rejected RMAs?</h2>\n  <p>The 4Phones RMA department occasionally faces RMAs that unfortunately must be denied. We have noticed the following inaccuracies. Make sure you take these points into account so that your RMA will not be rejected:</p>\n  <h3>1: Not Testing Before Installing</h3>\n  <p>It is important to test your products before using and installing them. Testing before installing helps you notice any defects in advance. Our RMA department is able to detect whether you tested products before installation.</p>\n  <h3>2: Wrong Placement of Flex Cables</h3>\n  <p>Our RMA department often comes across flex cable issues. Most of the products that get denied for RMA approval contain a damaged flex cable or connector. The damage is caused by incorrect placement during installation or bending of the flex cables. Ensure a very careful installation; any lack of precision could lead to a harmed product.</p>\n  <h3>3: Removal of Protective Foils</h3>\n  <p>The protective foils should not be removed before returning the products. Don’t remove any foils until sure it is going to be installed. Make sure the product is as close to its original state as possible (which includes the foils) before claiming the RMA.</p>\n  <h3>4: Incorrectly Packed Returns</h3>\n  <p>Products should be returned in a way that is closest to their original state. This means that RMAs should contain the original packaging. Another important thing regarding the packaging of the returned product is protection. Products should be carefully packed by using bubble foil, enough layers of carton or proper boxes. This way, we’ll more surely receive the package in the state in which you shipped it.</p>\n  <h3>5: Products Not Purchased from 4Phones</h3>\n  <p>Make sure that the returned product is 100% ours before shipping. We can tell by the visible and invisible markings what belongs to us and what doesn’t.</p>\n  <h3>6: Returning Without Mentioning the Problem or Defect</h3>\n  <p>Sometimes we receive products without a clear RMA reason. Therefore, it is important to clearly mention the problem or defect you’re facing. Give us as much information about the problem as you can, if applicable supported by photos and videos.</p>\n  <h3>7: RMA's Returned Without Correct Attachment of RMA Packing Slip Document as Received via Email</h3>\n  <p>It is important that the RMA is properly bundled with a clear RMA form, so that it’s easily recognizable which products belong to each RMA form.</p>\n\n  <h2>The Credit Process</h2>\n  <p>When your RMA is approved, you will receive a credit invoice that we offset against outstanding invoices or a refund in case there are no outstanding invoices.</p>\n\n  <h2>What if the Order Never Arrived?</h2>\n  <p>In case your order has not arrived, please contact our customer service.</p>\n<div>\n  <style>\n  .collapsible {\n    background-color: #eee;\n    color: #444;\n    cursor: pointer;\n    padding: 18px;\n    width: 100%;\n    border: none;\n    text-align: left;\n    outline: none;\n    font-size: 15px;\n  }\n\n  .active, .collapsible:hover {\n    background-color: #ccc;\n  }\n\n  .collapsible:after {\n    content: \"\\25B6\"; /* Unicode character for a right-pointing triangle */\n    font-size: 13px;\n    color: #777;\n    float: right;\n    margin-left: 5px;\n  }\n\n  .active:after {\n    content: \"\\25BC\"; /* Unicode character for a down-pointing triangle */\n  }\n\n  .content {\n    padding: 0 18px;\n    max-height: 0;\n    overflow: hidden;\n    transition: max-height 0.2s ease-out;\n    background-color: #f9f9f9;\n  }\n</style>\n\n<div>\n  <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\n\n  <button class=\"collapsible\">What Do I Have to Do to Return My Product(s)?</button>\n  <div class=\"content\">\n    <p>To return your product(s), follow these steps:</p>\n    <ol>\n      <li><strong>Submit the RMA</strong>: Log into your account, click on ‘My RMAs’, and request a new return. Select your order, choose the items, and provide the reason for return. Include additional information in the comments and/or attach a picture of the product to speed up processing.</li>\n      <li><strong>Wait for Approval</strong>: Wait for the RMA department to review and approve your return.</li>\n      <li><strong>Print and Send</strong>: Once approved, print the return form, add it to your package, and send it to:\n        <ul>\n          <li>De vest 34</li>\n          <li>5555 XP, Valkenswaard</li>\n          <li>The Netherlands</li>\n        </ul>\n      </li>\n      <li><strong>Confirmation and Tracking</strong>: You will receive a confirmation once we have received the package. You can track the status of your RMA in your account.</li>\n    </ol>\n    <p>Learn more about creating an RMA in our guide.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <button class=\"collapsible\">What Is the Status of My RMA?</button>\n  <div class=\"content\">\n    <p>You can always find the status of your return in your account. You will also receive status updates via email.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <button class=\"collapsible\">What Are the Return Conditions?</button>\n  <div class=\"content\">\n    <p>Ensure the following conditions are met for a successful return:</p>\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>Registration</strong>: Ensure the return is registered in your account.</li>\n      <li><strong>Pre-Installation Inspection</strong>: Customers must test and inspect the product before installation. Our RMA department can identify if a product has been installed.</li>\n      <li><strong>Clear Labeling</strong>: Clearly mark the outside of the box as an RMA shipment to expedite processing.</li>\n      <li><strong>Original Condition</strong>: Products must have been purchased from 4Phones and returned in their original condition and packaging. Avoid writing or placing stickers on products or packaging.</li>\n      <li><strong>No Damage</strong>: Products should not be damaged. The RMA department will assess the condition of returned products.</li>\n      <li><strong>Warranty Period</strong>: Note that all products have a specific warranty period, which varies by product group.</li>\n    </ul>\n  </div>\n\n  <button class=\"collapsible\">How Long Does It Take to Process My RMA?</button>\n  <div class=\"content\">\n    <p>We aim to process RMAs within 5 working days from receipt. During busy periods, this may take longer. Once processed, the refund will be issued as store credit within 2 business days.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <button class=\"collapsible\">What If the Package Is Damaged During Transport?</button>\n  <div class=\"content\">\n    <p>If a package arrives damaged, refuse it and inform our customer service. If you receive a defective product, contact us immediately. If you urgently need the goods, place a new order. We will increase your store credit once we receive the damaged items.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <button class=\"collapsible\">What Should I Do If I Have Received the Wrong Product?</button>\n  <div class=\"content\">\n    <p>If you received the wrong product, contact us within 5 working days so we can resolve the issue promptly.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <button class=\"collapsible\">What Happens to My Rejected Items?</button>\n  <div class=\"content\">\n    <p>Products rejected by the RMA department are automatically disposed of after 1 week. Contact us if you wish to have the product returned.</p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<script>\n  var coll = document.getElementsByClassName(\"collapsible\");\n  var i;\n\n  for (i = 0; i < coll.length; i++) {\n    coll[i].addEventListener(\"click\", function() {\n      this.classList.toggle(\"active\");\n      var content = this.nextElementSibling;\n      if (content.style.maxHeight){\n        content.style.maxHeight = null;\n      } else {\n        content.style.maxHeight = content.scrollHeight + \"px\";\n      } \n    });\n  }\n</script>\n</div>",
